If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder then every clinician should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient and should provide a naloxone-proper-use-overdose-reversal-training to the patient.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder and the patient has a household-member then every clinician should offer a naloxone-dose to the household-member and should provide a naloxone-proper-use-overdose-reversal-training to the household-member.
If a patient has an opioid-use-disorder and the patient has a significant-other then every clinician should offer a naloxone-dose to the significant-other and should provide a naloxone-proper-use-overdose-reversal-training to the significant-other.
